{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/496055-pact-equation-rules-question","id":496055,"title":"Pact Equation/Rules Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-29T01:30:52-07:00","id":496055,"title":"Pact Equation/Rules Question","content":"Suppose a Demon wants to secure, instead of a cult, or the other standard pact benefits, gaining reliable service in the form of Favors, should this be reflected mechanically?<br /> On the flip side, perhaps the one the Demon is offering a Pact to wants a Favor done for them, should this also be done mechanically?<br /> If done mechanically, should these merely be &quot;Contract is Broken, Benefits are Lost&quot; or should these be more compulsive in nature?<br /> <br /> The book makes a fair deal out of how Pacts with Vampires and other supernatural creatures are of limited utility, but having someone in your debt who is supernatural could easily be pretty potent, and I couldn't find any specific rules suggesting how to handle such a scenario(though I could have missed them, presumably)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5670-kalad2","name":"kalad2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:39:39-07:00","id":496257,"title":"","content":"There kind of IS a way to write in favors into a pact. There's no direct favor-for-favor trading, but the Interface book has details on making promissory pacts, where you can set certain dates or conditions for other parts of the pact to activate, and those conditions can include favors. Specific dates are worth 1 point, and any other condition are worth two points; it can be added or subtracted from the total, depending on whom the delay or condition favors.<br /> <br /> So, theoretically, two demons could set up a pact where they trade a favor for something else, and put up something as collateral. &quot;I will do X for you, or you get part of my Cover.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the book doesn't really say that the pacts with supernaturals are limited utility - it says a Demon can't use pacts to steal vampire, wolf, or mage powers. And soul pacts cause physical damage. This is just nothing more than basic no-template-crossing protection. There's absolutely nothing stopping you from using any of the rest of the stuff. Even more? There are a number of Embeds and Exploits that allow you to mimic being another supernatural, so you can take their lives over and pretend to be one. The damage-from-a-soul-theft is the only way that making a deal with a supernatural differs from dealing with a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:15:27-07:00","id":496674,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your time, and I was more talking about the general /tone/ of how they talked about pacts with other supernaturals in the core","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5670-kalad2","name":"kalad2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T17:10:04-07:00","id":496885,"title":"","content":"I got the feeling the general tone was &quot;no, you can't mess with supernatural powers/abilities via pact, that's the Embeds and Exploits are for.&quot; Treat other supernaturals like mortals. I didn't read any of that other stuff in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:32:19-07:00","id":497662,"title":"","content":"Demonic pacts are written to be very specific about what the Demon gets out of it - the developers have said before that it was explicitly written in a way to <i>not</i> reflect general magically enforced promises, a la Changeling's Pledges.<br /> <br /> You can do so at your table no problem, and the system as written has enough give that you don't necessarily have to go after just Cult or Cover stuff, but trading things for favor don't have any amount of the reality-warping that I see as a hallmark of the Pact system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 04-30-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T23:42:45-07:00","id":596560,"title":"","content":"Though, it does feel like tasks are supposed to be part of pacts, considering some of the things they imply demons do. Raise Dead and other powers read like they should be able to be used to create pacts. I kind of wonder if that isn't an accidental omission. Changeling Pledges are clearly meant to envoke a feeling akin to sacred promises from Celtic myth and fairy tales, so I get why they are different, but since demon pacts are supposed to be a transaction, services seem appropriate. 'I will bring him back from the dead, but only if this other takes his place...' that seems appropriately Faustian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1547-bunnirabbi","name":"BunniRabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1547_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T23:49:46-07:00","id":596568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BunniRabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/496055-pact-equation-rules-question?p=596560#post596560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, it does feel like tasks are supposed to be part of pacts, considering some of the things they imply demons do. Raise Dead and other powers read like they should be able to be used to create pacts. I kind of wonder if that isn't an accidental omission. Changeling Pledges are clearly meant to envoke a feeling akin to sacred promises from Celtic myth and fairy tales, so I get why they are different, but since demon pacts are supposed to be a transaction, services seem appropriate. 'I will bring him back from the dead, but only if this other takes his place...' that seems appropriately Faustian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conditional delay tags with the promissory pact rules added in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134224/Demon-Interface\" target=\"_blank\">Interface</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}